  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "there is a rendering issue where outlines on objects bleed or transpass into the opposite eye's field of view. This visual artifact occurs consistently across all objects, leading to a disorienting experience in VR.\n\nReproduction Steps:\n\n   Play VRChat in VR mode.\n\n   Position an pickup or interactable at the edge of the screen.\n\n   Observe that the outline effect transpasses into the opposite eye’s view, causing visual disruption.\n\nExpected Behavior: Outlines should render correctly and independently for each eye, without bleeding into the other eye’s view, \n\neven when objects are near the edge of the screen.\n\nObserved Behavior: The outline effect consistently transpasses into the opposite eye’s view when objects are at the edge of the \n\nscreen, as shown in the attached image.\n\nAdditional Notes: The issue does not seem to be dependent on the VR headset, as it persists across vr hardware. It is particularly \n\nnoticeable when using the Bigscreen Beyond headset.\n\nI haven't been able to test it on quest or pico\n\nHardware Specifications:\n\n Headset: Bigscreen Beyond\n\n GPU: NVIDIA RTX 4090\n\n Driver Version: 560.81\n\nAttachment: A screenshot of the issue is attached for reference.",
